      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best AI writing tool in 2026?</summary>
          <p>The best AI writing tool in 2026 depends on your use case. Claude (Anthropic) wins for long-form content, research, and accuracy on technical topics because of its 200k+ context window and lower hallucination rate on recent benchmarks. ChatGPT wins for broad accessibility, plugins/browsing, and DALL-E image integration. Grammarly wins as a writing assistant embedded in every editor you already use. Jasper wins for marketing teams that need campaign workflows and brand voices. Copy.ai wins as the best-value startup copy tool.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Claude or ChatGPT better for writing?</summary>
          <p>Claude is better for long-form writing, research-heavy content, and technical writing because its larger context window lets it ingest entire books, research papers, or product docs and maintain consistent style across very long outputs. ChatGPT is better for short-form copy, real-time web research via Browse, multi-modal (image + text) prompts, and plugin workflows. Most professional writers use both: Claude for drafting long pieces, ChatGPT for ideation, research, and refinement.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are AI writing tools worth paying for?</summary>
          <p>Yes for anyone writing more than 2–3 hours per week. Claude Pro ($20/mo), ChatGPT Plus ($20/mo), Grammarly Premium ($12–$15/mo), and Jasper Business ($49+/seat/mo) each pay for themselves in 2–4 hours of saved drafting, editing, or research time per month. Freelance writers, content teams, marketers, and students all report measurable ROI. For casual users writing under 1 hour per week, the free tiers of ChatGPT, Claude, and Grammarly are usually sufficient.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can AI writing tools produce SEO-optimized content?</summary>
          <p>Yes, when combined with a human editor and SEO workflow. Jasper and Copy.ai have native SEO modes powered by Surfer SEO or Frase integrations. Claude and ChatGPT can write optimally structured content if prompted with target keywords, outlines, and competitor SERPs. However, AI-only content without human fact-checking, editorial review, and original reporting/quotes typically performs poorly on Google in 2026 because the Helpful Content System prioritizes experience, expertise, and original analysis over generated prose. Use AI as a drafting and editing assistant — not as a publisher.</p>
        </details>
